---
module: contracts-verification
func_id: verify-contracts
---

***conformance tests***

# stages-fixtures-before-testing
Given an empty fixture directory and a Cargo stand-in that writes a distinct marker for each program and hook variant, when `make -j4 verify` runs, then Cargo's test command sees all four markers under their corresponding fixture filenames, followed by the formatting and lint checks.

***acceptance tests***

# stops-after-failure
Given a Cargo stand-in that can fail at a selected build or check, when `make verify` reaches that failure, then Make exits with a failure and no later Cargo command runs.
